<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Italy</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of San Marco</h1><p class="st-meta">1848 CE – 1849 CE · capital Venice</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The revolutionary Venetian republic of 1848–1849 led by Daniele Manin, which held out against an Austrian siege for seventeen months.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>As revolution spread across <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>, crowds freed the lawyer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniele-manin">Daniele Manin</a> from prison on 17 March 1848, and on 22 March the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venetians</a> rose against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-lombardy-venetia">Kingdom of Lombardy-Venetia</a> and took the Arsenal. Manin proclaimed the Republic of San Marco, reviving the name of the old <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-venice">Republic of Venice</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniele-manin">Manin</a> led the government, with the writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niccolo-tommaseo">Niccolò Tommaseo</a> among its ministers. The republic briefly voted in July 1848 to join the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-sardinia">Kingdom of Sardinia</a>, but after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/piedmont">Piedmont's</a> defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-custoza-1848">Custoza</a> it returned to independence. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venetians</a> raised loans, printed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paper-money">paper money</a> and organised a national guard and defence of the lagoon, which became a symbol of Italian resistance.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Austrian forces besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> from 1849, bombarding the city while cholera and hunger spread. The republic surrendered in August 1849, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daniele-manin">Manin</a> went into exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetia">Venetia</a> joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-italy">Kingdom of Italy</a> in 1866.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-san-marco.jpg" alt="Republic of San Marco" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: Facquis · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Republic_of_Saint_Mark.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1848 CE – 1849 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Venice</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Daniele Manin, Niccolò Tommaseo</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Venetian, Italian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Republic of Saint Mark, Repubblica di San Marco</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1848&amp;focus=republic-of-san-marco" aria-label="Republic of San Marco on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4973 575 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of San Marco lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5293 831L5218 830M5293 831L5381 747"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5218 830h0M5381 747h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5293 831h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5293 831h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Venice. <a href="/atlas?year=1848&amp;focus=republic-of-san-marco">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
